  "goodToKnow": "Die Patientenverfügung is a living will or advance directive, stating which medical treatments one wants or refuses if no longer able to decide, for example life support. Since 2009, it has been legally binding in Germany if written and specific enough. It's often combined with a Vorsorgevollmacht (lasting power of attorney) for a trusted person. Plural: die Patientenverfügungen."
